- The little mood noises of the character (purr, giggle, growl, mrrp, kiss, sneeze, yawn, chime,
  the hurt meow for sadness, whistle and the child's laugh) are real recordings from the Mixkit
  free sound library (https://mixkit.co/), used under the Mixkit free licence
  (https://mixkit.co/license/), which allows free use, including commercial use, without attribution.
  They voice the faces gallery and accent moments elsewhere; the home character, the doll in
  settings and the floating head are silent by design, and nothing is played on silent/vibrate/Do-Not-Disturb.
  Mood cues of the scripted show bypass quiet-mode on the owner's order. The exact clips and their source pages:
    purr.mp3      — "Sphinx cat purr"                  (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/cats/)          sfx id 3091
    mrrp.mp3      — "Sweet kitty meow"                (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/cats/)          sfx id 93
    growl.mp3     — "Angry wild cat roar"             (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/cats/)          sfx id 89
    sad.mp3       — "Little cat pain meow"            (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/cats/)          sfx id 87
    giggle.mp3    — "Kid giggle laugh"                (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/giggle/)        sfx id 431
    laugh.mp3     — "Happy child laughing"            (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/laugh/)         sfx id 2265
    kiss.mp3      — "Little cute kiss"                (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/kisses/)        sfx id 2192
    sneeze.mp3    — "Adult sneeze"                    (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/sneeze/)        sfx id 2212
    yawn.mp3      — "Young tired male yawns"          (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/yawn/)          sfx id 2278
    whistle.mp3   — "Male gentle whistle"             (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/whistle/)       sfx id 612
    chime.mp3     — "Relaxing bell chime"             (https://mixkit.co/free-sound-effects/bell/)          sfx id 3109
  All of them were loudness-normalised to about −21 LUFS, converted to mono, and are stored
  in app/src/main/res/raw/. The script that re-downloads and re-normalises them is
  tools/fetch_sounds.sh.
